    {
        "content": "<h1>roc for scripting</h1>\n<p>I experimented with roc for scripting and want to share my thoughts and experience.</p>\n<p>I replaced a 10 line posix shell script and a more complex janet script with roc.</p>\n<p>original posix script:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"ch\">#!/bin/sh</span>\n\n<span class=\"nv\">tmpTYPSTFile</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"/tmp/typst2pdf</span><span class=\"nv\">$$</span><span class=\"s2\">.typ\"</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">tmpPDFFile</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"/tmp/typst2pdf</span><span class=\"nv\">$$</span><span class=\"s2\">.pdf\"</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">trap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'rm -f -- \"$tmpTYPSTFile\" \"$tmpPDFFile\"'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>EXIT<span class=\"w\"> </span>TERM<span class=\"w\"> </span>INT<span class=\"w\"> </span>QUIT\n\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>-t<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">printf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"%s: stdin not provided\\n\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"nv\">$0</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>&gt;<span class=\"p\">&amp;</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">exit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\ncat<span class=\"w\"> </span>&gt;<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"nv\">$tmpTYPSTFile</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span>\n\ntypst<span class=\"w\"> </span>compile<span class=\"w\"> </span>--pdf-standard<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">2</span>.0<span class=\"w\"> </span>--format<span class=\"o\">=</span>pdf<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"nv\">$tmpTYPSTFile</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"nv\">$tmpPDFFile</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span>\n\ncat<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"nv\">$tmpPDFFile</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>same script in roc</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Ruby\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"ch\">#!/usr/bin/env roc</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">app</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">main!</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"ss\">pf</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">platform</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://codeberg.org/removewingman/restricted-roc/releases/download/v0.2.0/DP5N5ev2nXZ1XSKWHPQZnjSLz5CmfCxYm3QAfrrMxoWR.tar.zst\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Stdin</span>\n<span class=\"n\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Stdout</span>\n<span class=\"n\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Stderr</span>\n<span class=\"n\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Script</span>\n<span class=\"n\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">File</span>\n<span class=\"n\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pf</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Process</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">main!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"no\">Script</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">stdin_provided_else_exit!</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">message</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"${args.get(0)?}: stdin not provided\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">})?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">input_file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">File</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">create_bytes_tmp!</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">name</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"typst2pdf\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">extension</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"typ\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">bytes_content</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">Stdin</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bytes!</span><span class=\"p\">()?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">})?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">output_file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">File</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tmp_name!</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">name</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"typst2pdf\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">extension</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"pdf\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">})?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">Process</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">run!</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">bin</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"typst\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">args</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"compile --pdf-standard 2.0 --format=pdf ${input_file} ${output_file}\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">})?</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">success_and_stderr_empty</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">error_message</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"typst error\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"no\">Ok</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">File</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">content_bytes!</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">absolute_path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">output_file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">})?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"no\">Stdout</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">write_bytes!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"no\">Err</span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">exit_write_to_stderr!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://codeberg.org/removewingman/plainaipha/pulls/1\">janet script pr</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What I like</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>similar to janet<ul>\n<li>both writing a script in one file and expanding into multiple files if it gets to much are possible and can turn into a binary</li>\n<li>compile time checks, type interference</li>\n<li>feels simple and smooth</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>import exposing</li>\n<li><code>!</code>, <code>?</code>, <code>dbg</code> and <code>crash</code></li>\n<li>string handling and multiline strings</li>\n<li>descriptive error handling and easy of use to introduce new errors</li>\n<li>ability to scope into mutability</li>\n<li>not having Optionals</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What I am unsure about / could be better</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>implementation of <code>trap</code> functionality<ul>\n<li>platform tracks tmp files and deletes them after program execution, feels right not sure tho</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>platform api (I implemented this, but could change lol)</li>\n<li>builtins for the <code>!</code> and <code>try?</code> functions, e.g. <code>for_each_try!</code></li>\n<li>importing multiple things like so <code>import pf.[Stdin, Stdout]</code> (anything so 10 lines are not wasted on imports)</li>\n<li>shadowing local variables bindings inside a function scope (I know this has been discussed, just want to state my experience)<ul>\n<li>every popular scripting language (Python/Janet/Lua/Ruby) has this feature, I missed it</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>structural records to have defaults</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>tmp_name! : { name: Str, extension: Str, automatically_delete: Bool ?? true } =&gt; Try({}, [FileCreateErr(Str)])\n</code> (throws compile error)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>roc works on more unix systems e.g. FreeBSD/OpenBSD</p>\n</li>\n<li>smaller, simpler and more clear error and warning compiler messages when using check</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Would I use roc to replace a 10 line posix script? Probably not.</li>\n<li>Would I use roc to write a bit more complex scripts instead of Janet/Python/Ruby/Lua ? Absolutely. <ul>\n<li>obv. for e.g. a river wm there has to be the <a href=\"https://codeberg.org/river/tinyrwm/src/branch/main/janet\">ecosystem</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Would I like roc more as a config language instead of Lua/Toml/Janet? Definitely.<ul>\n<li>afaik, it is already one of roc's goals to be as easy embeddable as Janet/Lua</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Let me know what you think :)</p>",
        "id": 634142764,
